    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4446" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλο-δαπός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλοδ-</span>, cf. Lat.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>aliud</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-απος</span>
			=
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ṇθ[υγλιδε]<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span></span>, cf. Lat. <i>long-inquus) belonging
				to another people</i> or <i>land, foreign</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.550
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.485
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1082
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.7.14
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀλλοδαπῇ</span>”
				<i>in foreign parts,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sammelb.
					4284.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span> :— later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλο-δᾰπής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				68.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ps.-Callisth.
				2.21
			</span></i>.</div>
